{"nodes": [{"id": "supabase_policies_product_prices_product_prices_deny_all", "label": "product_prices RLS posture (deny-all, FINAL)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/policies/product_prices.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "FINAL deny-all (card ^ref-12). NO SELECT POLICY LANDS: reads arrive only through v_config_history, SECURITY DEFINER, carrying `where fn_current_role() = 'L1_OWNER'` (R34, R20). This is the purest case of L3 price-blindness \u2014 the table is nothing but dated prices, so any table-level policy would be a second read path around the owner-only WHERE and would hand prices to L2 and L3 through PostgREST. Never `force row level security` here or on profiles."}, {"id": "concept_no_second_read_path", "label": "No second read path: a table policy would bypass the view's owner-only WHERE", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "supabase/policies/product_prices.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "supabase_policies_product_prices_product_prices_deny_all", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000004_stock_and_branch_daily_product_prices", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/policies/product_prices.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_policies_product_prices_product_prices_deny_all", "target": "concept_deny_all_rls_posture", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/policies/product_prices.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_policies_product_prices_product_prices_deny_all", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_current_role_fn_current_role", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/policies/product_prices.sql", "so